- sessionless: no session id → `.fah/trajectories/sessionless/requests/`.
- rotation maxBytes: store with maxBytes small; write 3 blobs; expect oldest deleted; remaining total ≤ maxBytes; newest kept.
- TTL: files with old mtime (setMtime) get deleted on next write/enforce.
- write returns null on failure: construct store with a FileSystem that fails writes? MemoryExecutionEnv with a failing shell isn't enough. Look for an existing failing-fs test helper... `grep -rn "class FailingFs\|writeBinaryFile.*Err" test/ | head`. I'll check; if none, skip that case or build a tiny failing wrapper in the test (implement FileSystem by delegating — the interface has ~15 members; a `_FailWritesFs` wrapper implementing FileSystem via forwarding is verbose but doable. Alternative: `env.writeFile` to an invalid path? MemoryExecutionEnv may allow any path. Let me instead test the WRITE-failure contract through a wrapper class implementing `FileSystem` + `Shell`… Actually `ExecutionEnv` = FileSystem + Shell. I can wrap a MemoryExecutionEnv with a class implementing ExecutionEnv that forwards everything (noSuchMethod forwarding!). Dart noSuchMethod can implement the interface tersely:

```dart
class _FailWritesEnv implements ExecutionEnv {
 _FailWritesEnv(this._inner);
 final ExecutionEnv _inner;
 @override
 dynamic noSuchMethod(Invocation invocation) {
 if (invocation.memberName == #writeBinaryFile || invocation.memberName == #writeFile) {
  return Future.value(Err(const FileError(...)));
 }
 return Function.apply(...)? 
 }
``
noSuchMethod forwarding to _inner: `return Reflect...` — dart:mirror banned. Cleaner: explicit forward for the used members. Let me check `FileError` shape and whether tests already have such a wrapper — search.

